-- ============================================================================
-- DC20 - Mapping PROFESSIONAL (intermediate tier) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (mapping, intermediate) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its ACTIVE
-- academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/mapping/intermediate/manifest.json (the structure source
-- of truth; emitted by a generator, not hand-typed), and seeding the six module
-- quiz banks plus the final exam. Answer keys live only here and in the table.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the mapping teaching oracle and reproduces the
-- live NG6 Professional capstone answer key: the Ekene SAND isochore, BASE_SAND
-- gridded on the TOP_SAND frame and subtracted node for node. Minimum 25 m,
-- maximum 35.897705078125 m, map mean 32.25429068038713 m, thickness at prospect
-- P-1 34.050048828125 m, 201 live nodes graded exactly, and a plain well mean of
-- 31.166666666666668 m. Same pipeline src/lib/mappingTeaching.js drives and
-- isochoreLab.test.js pins, on the shared @petrolord/engines gridding engines.
--
-- Tier note: the Associate tier (DC8) owns the frame, the spline, the mask, the
-- crest problem, the contour rule and the reading at P-1, and this tier does not
-- re-teach them. It owns the second surface, grid arithmetic, how the two masks
-- interact, the linearity result that makes subtract-then-grid and
-- grid-then-subtract the same answer, the two honest means and their
-- decomposition, thickness at a prospect and gross rock volume. Leave-one-out,
-- the blind test and the jackknife belong to the Expert tier (DC21).
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked
-- for cyclic key sequences and within-pool near-duplicates before seeding, per
-- DC12 and DC13. Every bank is 4/4/4/3 on answer index.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert, so
-- learners enrolled before this apply finish on the old path; the ON CONFLICT
-- update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on re-seeds. Re-seeding
-- replaces the whole bank for this course-tier; fine while there are no open
-- attempts (open attempts pin question ids).
--
-- Ladder note: an INTERMEDIATE enrollment needs an unrevoked ASSOCIATE
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop a mapping
-- associate cert in-transaction, and a probe confirms the tier below
-- (mapping, beginner) is left undisturbed at 132 questions.
--
-- NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

values ('mapping', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-a-second-surface","title":"A Second Surface","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-the-base-sand-picks","l03-one-frame-two-surfaces","l04-the-isochore-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-subtracting-grids","title":"Subtracting Grids","lesson_keys":["l01-node-for-node-arithmetic","l02-the-masks-interact","l03-two-routes-to-one-answer","l04-honouring-the-wells","l05-isochore-and-isopach"]},{"key":"m03-reading-the-thickness-map","title":"Reading the Thickness Map","lesson_keys":["l01-the-thickness-extremes","l02-the-thick-spot-is-not-the-crest","l03-thickness-at-the-prospect","l04-the-contour-interval-changes","l05-cell-size-and-the-thickness-map"]},{"key":"m04-two-honest-means","title":"Two Honest Means","lesson_keys":["l01-the-well-mean","l02-the-map-mean","l03-why-they-differ","l04-which-one-to-quote"]},{"key":"m05-what-an-isochore-is-for","title":"What an Isochore is For","lesson_keys":["l01-gross-rock-volume","l02-feeding-volumetrics","l03-thickness-as-geology","l04-where-a-thickness-map-lies"]},{"key":"m06-the-isochore-workflow","title":"The Isochore Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-onward-to-expert"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
